Good morning,

I'm writing with concern about Thorwin Properties non-compliance with fire =
related procedure and protocol.

On January 14 around 7 pm the main building fire alarm was triggered. It co=
ntinued until a tenant called 911 in order to alert the fire department who=
 can only turn off the alarm at the building. The issue appears to be a fai=
lure in compliance in which the tenant responsible for the smoke produced b=
y burning food was not informed about fire safety procedure and protocol. I=
n addition, the reason for the main alarm system being triggered is due to =
the tenant being unable to open the windows in their suite and allow exit f=
or the smoke.

The tenant in question is a family of newcomers and they should not be held=
 responsible for their ignorance of procedure when language difficulties ar=
e a factor. Fire safety protocol documentation do not appear to be availabl=
e through Thorwin Properties, and if they do exist, they were not communica=
ted to the tenant in an effective manner, endangering the safety of the com=
munity and requiring me to take an active role in the protection of the com=
munity by organizing response.

An investigation is needed into the building's alarm system and its communi=
cation with authorities and signage and documentation necessary to inform t=
enants of protocol and procedure. My understanding is that the alarm does n=
ot communicate its triggering with the authorities and it is required that =
the tenants contact 911 in order to call the fire department and have the o=
fficers come to turn off the alarm.

The property manager, Grant Steele, arrived at the exact same time as the f=
ire response team and did not check in with all building residents to confi=
rm that there was no danger after the alarm was turned off.

It appears that Thorwin Properties does not have an effective plan or commu=
nication of plan for procedure and this constitutes a serious safety issue =
for the tenants of the building. It also appears that the windows are a saf=
ety issue and their functioning needs to be assessed.

Thank you,
Evan Rosner
10-585 Corydon Ave
R3L0P3
2048991499

